		<div class="row mb-5 justify-content-between">
			<div class="col-lg-6 text-black-100 order-lg-2">
				<p>
					"The Sandman" is an American fantasy drama TV and audiobook series based on the 1989–1996 comic book written by Neil Gaiman and published by DC Comics. The series was developed by Gaiman, David S. Goyer, and Allan Heinberg for the streaming service Netflix and is produced by DC Entertainment and Warner Bros. Television. The Sandman tells the story of Dream/Morpheus, the titular Sandman.
				</p>
				<p>
					In the TV series, the character Nimrod is portrayed by Kerry Shale. He appears in Season 1 in three episodes: S01E07 "The Doll's House", S01E09 "Collectors", and S01E10 "Lost Hearts". Season 2 will be the final season of The Sandman.
				</p>
				<p>
					In the audiobook series, directed by multiple award-winning Dirk Maggs, Kerry Shale voices a variety of characters, including Abel, Azazel, Brute, Creeper, Etrigan, Harold Smith, Lee, Marsh, Monk, Puck, Scott Free, and Security Guard #2. Acts I to III are available on Audible and Amazon, either as a download or on MP3 CDs.<br />
					The production of Act IV was completed in early 2024, while Act V was still in progress. However, the release of both Act IV and Act V has been put on hold, leaving their future uncertain.
				</p>
				<p>
					Please follow Dirk Maggs on Bluesky. <br />
					- <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/dirkmaggs.bsky.social" target="_blank">Dirk Maggs on Bluesky</a><br />
				</p>
